  "rationale": "The representative prefix ends in “with,” but the model assigns most mass to the determiner “a”; the Mia root lacks the useful post-“with” proper-noun rule present in other name roots. Add that contextual evidence for Mia without asserting that every “with” must introduce a person. Across the batch, several noun targets follow adjectives (including small pears/scissors/needles, small apples, sunny day, little village, and next time), while those continuations are weakly supported. Add modest adjective-suffix evidence to those noun roots. Other continuations remain possible, and the broader noun evidence may also favor a noun in contexts where an adjective is followed by something else; replay evaluation should check that tradeoff.",
